sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg wavelength at the 1.178 mm shell-thickness tier of Aptenodytes forsteri — MorphoEval overall 88.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 overall 88.3. Remediation items from pass 1 are closed in the script: robust display, scale sweep, equal-diffusion ablation, specimen segmentation, and goodness-of-fit (r=0.9979, RMSE=0.0301 mm, KS=0.143). The GIF terminal frame matches the MHNT egg (CV 84.7, 16 frames, 640 px). The generative wavelength remains 1.178 mm and is not forced onto the 0.66 mm pore measurement. No second assessor. Nanopub signing profile was absent. Overall 88.3/100 (faithfulness 87.8, reproducibility 89.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 95244113b1348dfeec9466cf094db251e2807d75; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/aptenodytes_forsteri_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 95244113b1348dfeec9466cf094db251e2807d75, image/png, 259363 B, 1464×648 px, artifact_sha256 4a0ff4289fae61fc4874e6ee493314e76e29174e2b0d8d624c673cdf12806435 (sha256 4a0ff4289fae61fc4874e6ee493314e76e29174e2b0d8d624c673cdf12806435), spec_fingerprint 8258983b5a6bcf70e050b83d480003ff7d17bbb90cda5744e49bb2bec31fced1. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 8258983b5a6bcf70e050b83d480003ff7d17bbb90cda5744e49bb2bec31fced1; artifact_sha256: 4a0ff4289fae61fc4874e6ee493314e76e29174e2b0d8d624c673cdf12806435; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/aptenodytes_forsteri_turing_wavelength_s0/aptenodytes_forsteri_specimen.jpg=70b89e84383c36f8...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Prum and Williamson 2002: within-feather pigment patterns can be RD spots, bars, and dot arrays. | Chinese Journal of Polar Research 2008: emperor egg 121.3 by 83.8 mm, shell thickness 1.11 mm (0.94-1.32).; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics a=0.20, b=0.30, D_v/D_u=42, with D_u set so the fastest mode is 10^(-2.929) m. | Commensurate-scale sweep comparing dispersion wavelength to the PDE Fourier peak. | Median-to-99.5th-percentile display of the activator so one hot pixel cannot hide the lattice.; transfer_boundary: Shell thickness is a through-shell length. Using it as the lateral wavelength is a scale identification for this tier, not a published pore-spacing measurement.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the MHNT photograph's 0.66 mm pore FFT equals lambda_c. | Does not claim body-scale black-white countershading is a 1.178 mm Turing mode. | Does not claim a predecessor chronospecies; the series length is 1. | Sibling slot 119 parameters (alpha 1.31) are not used.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.883"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder and assessor, single-agent round; no second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

